t his  control and starts to even hurt those  around him  as a result yuta starts to keep to  himself becoming shy and quiet however  this unfortunately leads to him being  bullied  we only really see one example of this  but it's pretty gruesome yuta begs for  the bully to stop for his own safety but  the bully just ignores him and as he  goes on to harass utah rika emerges and  crams the bully as well as three other  children all inside one locker and it  really does seem like she would have to  play a lot of tetris with their bodies  to make them fit this believe it or not  draws attention to yuta and leads us to  the first scene of jiu jitsu kaizen zero  where he is brought into a room with  gojo very similar to how yuji had been  in the main series  as gojo enters he finds a knife that is  bent and mangled and yuta explains that  he tried to end his own life but rika  just won't let him  he is terrified of hurting others and  committed himself to isolation since he  can't end his own life gojo asks if he's  going to be lonely by himself and  instead asks if he'd rather come and  learn how to control rika instead of  just throwing his life away and with  that yuta joins the jiu-jitsu school in  a very similar fashion to how yuji had  he's brought to meet his classmates who  end up being toge panda and maki and the  second that the door opens all three of  them pick up on rika and launch their  feet ready to attack luckily gojo is  able to calm them down though before  rika emerges to kill them something  which in true gojo fashion he forgot to  warn them of yuta again just like yuji  is set up with a partner to go on his  first mission again dealing with some  missing children from a school that  suspects curses are to blame he and maki  arrive to clear out the curses most of  whom are small fries which makes this a  great first mission for him  we also briefly go into curse grades  where we learn that yuta is one of only  four special grade sorcerers along with  gojo which i mean you saw rika that  checks out to me we don't really get too  much time to focus on this though as a  massive curse appears throwing both of  them into the air and swallowing them  inside the curse's stomach they find the  missing children and we see maki's leg  is wounded and festering with curse  energy she asked yuta why he joined the  school in the first place and he said  that he wanted to gain confidence and  feel like he's allowed to live and she  tells him that if he wants to gain  confidence that he needs to do things  that mean something for example  defeating curses and now is the time to  act he calls upon rika for the first  time intentionally and the monstrous  curse easily defeats the gigantic enemy  even gojo is thrown off by rika's power  the cursed girl smiles and asks yuta if  he loves her only to notice that he is  gone and carrying maki to gojo for help  along the way the human form of rika  minus the top half of her head appears  behind him to cheer him on yuta begins  to remember more of what happened and  starts to think that maybe rika wasn't  the one to curse him but instead it  might be the other way around and gojo  says it's unclear but love is the most  twisted curse of all so anything is  possible and here you to vows to release  rika from her curse meanwhile much like  the higher ups are against yuji it seems  they're also against utah as well and  again we see gojo taking a guardian role  vouching for yuta he says it's better to  let him live so they can learn from rika  as she's a very unique case in honesty  while gojo might be interested in this  to some degree he is more interested in  making sure that no one's youth is  wasted or taken from them regardless of  the situation as gojo leaves one of the  higher ups warn him that the execution  of yuta is only on hold and gojo  responds if it comes to that i will side  with yuta with one of the most  terrifying glances that he's ever given  yuta starts training with maki which is  probably one of the best teachers you  can have and gojo gives him a katana so  that he can learn to use rika's power  pouring small amounts of it into the  blade at a time to practice as he learns  to slowly undo the curse this leads into  a pretty fun set of training sessions  with maki and of course panda asking  yuta if he likes big or small boobs to  see if maki has a chance it's a really  light fun and wholesome section but it  isn't long before another mission pops  up and gojo sends toge to deal with it  asking yuta to join and watch so he can  learn that said he is given the warning  not to let rika out because if he does  everyone will likely die which is the  closest i've ever seen to gojo admitting  that someone else might be stronger than  him the expectation in general for this  mission was a lot of curses to be  present but for them to be fairly weak  most of them were pretty easy for toki  to take out all at once that is until a  much more powerful curse arrives toge  originally wants to take him on himself  but yuta steps up and wanted to help he  starts to approach the curse and rika is  in full horror rage mode he channels her  into his katana and we see him moving  around in a confident and fast paced way  which really shows off how much his  training is paying off even with that  though he just still isn't strong enough  yet despite that he does manage to  create an opening for toge and together  they are able to take this monster down  this extra strong curse wasn't just a  random occurrence though as the next  panel shows ghetto who seems to have  released it into this area intentionally  speaking of ghetto we get a look at his  perspective and his plans in particular  we have a few scenes with him  demonstrating how he views non-sorcerers  as monkeys who are either to supply him  with money or curse spirits and if they  can't get him either of those they might  as well die in fact his overall plan is  just to wage a war where they will  annihilate all non-sorcerers and he  isn't alone in this he has a whole group  that he calls his family who are in it  with him finally we also get a look at  how his abilities work with him having a  black ball that he can use to absorb or  release demons essentially like a cursed  pokemon master he's soon after this  arrives at the school to confront utah  asking him to join their cause  he ultimately wants to kill yuta to take  his costa rica unfortunately though he  made the mistake of insulting maki which  upsets yuta to the point of knocking  ghetto away he then explains that he  can't help anyone who would belittle his  friends  gojo then asks ghetto why he's even here  and ghetto explains that he's declaring  war explaining that on december 24th he  will march 1 000 kurd spirits onto  shinjuku to kill every non-sorcerer  finally the day of the war arrives and  while maki and utah are at the school  everyone else seems to have gone to  shinjuku the pair has a bit of time to  talk and maki explains that she is  considered a failure because she has no  cursed energy so her goal is to become a  powerful sorcerer go back home and see  their faces when she proves them wrong  which to yuta is an inspiration saying  that he wants to live as strongly as she  does which if it wasn't for the ending  of this manga would be enough to make me  start shipping these two together as she  gets very flustered for being accepted  we don't get to focus on this too much  though as ghetto arrives at the school  and places a curtain around it the whole  explanation for an attack on shinjuku  was just set up to get everyone else  away from utah and it worked gojo  realizes what is happening and he sends  toge and panda back to the school with  some warp ring that he made on the floor  hoping that they can help against ghetto  as he takes everyone else on here and  together maki panda and toge totally  take ghetto down and save the day by  which i mean that they get absolutely  rocked and ghetto wins with little to no  effort yuta arrives and finds his  friends laid out on the ground sending  him into an absolute rage and calling  rika to battle as both he and ghetto say  that they will kill each other the  battle kicks off and rika grabs maki  however it seems like yuta is able to  control her much better now as he calls  her off what's interesting is seeing  rika's reaction to this immediately  apologizing on repeat and begging you to  not to be mad at her as she starts  crying he calms her down and instead  sends her to fight ghetto as he starts  to heal maki once maki is safe he asks  rika to follow his movements and it's an  all-out battle ghetto has tons of curses  everywhere zarika summons a megaphone  with toge's curse ability imbued into it  and yuta calls out telling them all to  die from here they swap to a  hand-to-hand fight and it is wild  everything is incredibly fast-paced  until utah's sword breaks and before  ghetto can finish talking down to him  yuta lands a massive punch pushed into a  corner ghetto decides to pull out all of  the stops he summons an imaginary  vengeful spirit and then combines all of  his nearly forty five hundred other  curses  into one abomination utah two makes his  next move as he turns to rika and hugs  her he thanks her for protecting him and  asks her to lend her power one more time  promising to give his life to her after  this battle so that they can be together  forever he says he loves her they kiss  and rika basically evolves calling out  how much she loves him together they  fire off one final blast and wipe  ghetto's curses out entirely ghetto is  insanely injured at this point but he  manages to get away from the fight where  he is found by gojo ghetto laughed  saying that he essentially sent panda  and toge to their death however gojo  says that he just simply trusted ghetto  to not kill young sorcerers so he knew  that panda and the others would most  likely be safe however in 